rClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes 3 attempts in total.\n\n**Behaviour:**\n- Only HTTP 503 triggers a retry. Any other HTTP error, such as a 500, is raised right away. Network errors (`URLError`) and timeouts are also not retried, since the request only mentioned 503.\n- The wait doubles each time: 0.5s before the second attempt, then 1s before the third.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised to the caller.\n- The 503 response is closed before retrying, so connections aren't left open.\n- `max_attempts=3` and `backoff_base=0.5` are new constructor arguments. Existing calls work unchanged because these defaults apply.\n\n**Tested** against a real local HTTP server (with `backoff_base=0.01` to keep it fast):\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 \u00d7 503, then 200 | data returned | 3 |\n| 3 \u00d7 503 | `HTTPError 503` raised | 3 |\n| 1 \u00d7 500 | `HTTPError 500` raised | 1 |\n| 200 | data returned | 1 |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add a test file. The check above was a one-off run, not a committed test.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 71510, "requests_cache_write": 107385, "requests_cost_usd": 0.587035, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1788, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial23", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 104, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:51:23.060866+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 57.47, "t_checker_s": 1.928, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_